{"candidates":[{"analogy":{"adopted_commitment_refs":[],"disanalogies":["Software schemas can be iterated and versioned instantly, whereas changing building codes requires legislative processes.","A software adapter failure results in data loss or pause, whereas a building code failure can result in physical catastrophe."],"overturn_conditions":["If the research involves physically dangerous experiments where software latency directly correlates to human safety, custom real-time systems may override standard protocols.","If the 'standard building codes' (existing trackers) are proven to be fundamentally incompatible with the laws of physics governing the new domain (novel AI paradigms)."],"shared_structure":["Both domains face a choice between adopting a standardized framework (building codes/existing trackers) with strict compliance (schema-first) versus designing a bespoke solution from scratch.","In both cases, the 'custom' route introduces high maintenance liability and risk of structural failure (fragility) for small teams.","The 'adapter' in software corresponds to 'pre-fabricated components' in construction: they allow custom designs to fit within standard safety frameworks."],"source_memory_refs":["Civil Engineering: Building codes vs. Custom Foundations"],"transfer_claims":["Just as small architecture firms rarely write their own structural physics engines, small research teams should not write their own persistence layers.","The 'Schema-First' contract offers the same liability protection in data science that building codes offer in civil engineering."]},"checker_specs":[],"claim":"For a small team building a research tool with active learning loops, the optimal path is to adopt an existing experiment tracker but enforce a 'Schema-First' contract via a lightweight adapter layer, rather than building a custom tracker from scratch.","counterconditions":["The active learning loop requires sub-second latency feedback that no existing tool's API can support without custom kernel modifications.","The research workflow is so novel that no existing schema ontology can represent the state transitions without losing causal fidelity.","The team possesses unique domain expertise in building distributed state machines but lacks the bandwidth to maintain compatibility with evolving third-party tracker APIs."],"discharges":[],"evidence_refs":[{"block":"4e4e9dcbcafb2b6d828f5d05a420396c12dd2354c85f57420230caa045a0b419","quote":"Adopt an existing tracker but enforce a 'Schema-First' contract: no data is logged until a formal schema (JSON Schema or Protobuf) is defined and versioned"}],"mechanism":"The mechanism is 'Constrained Integration': by defining a strict JSON Schema or Protobuf definition before any data is logged (the 'Schema-First' contract), the team eliminates the 'integration tax' of mismatched workflows and prevents the 'migration cliff' of unstructured noise. The adapter layer acts as a causal firewall, translating the specific requirements of the active learning loop into the generic events of the existing tool, thereby preserving the 'Separation of Concerns' without introducing a fragile custom state machine as a single point of failure.","optional_refs":["4e4e9dcbcafb2b6d828f5d05a420396c12dd2354c85f57420230caa045a0b419","88c48351e12d4c74c72a50c8486117653d11f5929d5c13f4961565c52ca4dcfb","0a5bd84458b8d1b8a2aae76319e4adaf0cffa9c60b2e788c9e29a24631924ec8"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["4e4e9dcbcafb2b6d828f5d05a420396c12dd2354c85f57420230caa045a0b419","88c48351e12d4c74c72a50c8486117653d11f5929d5c13f4961565c52ca4dcfb","0a5bd84458b8d1b8a2aae76319e4adaf0cffa9c60b2e788c9e29a24631924ec8"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.65}],"simulation_proposals":[]}